# The tables that pieces landing side by side each add lines to: a rebase keeps both sides' lines, main's first,
# instead of stopping. A line both sides changed is then kept twice, which the build refuses as a second function or
# the gates as a second row, and a line one side took out comes back as a call nothing calls or a row the check of
# ported files refuses. A table read as a set or a map would take such a line silently, so none is listed here.
doltgrust.tsv	merge=union
pg/calls.list	merge=union
pg/test-calls.list	merge=union
